  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A chunky throw is a 90 x 110 cm piece of plain double crochet worked back and forth in chunky-weight yarn on an 8 mm hook. The thick yarn builds height quickly: the full throw takes around 110 rows, which is a few hours of steady work rather than a multi-day project. The dense dc fabric in chunky yarn is noticeably heavier and warmer than a treble blanket in DK."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chunky wool or wool-blend gives the best drape and warmth; chunky acrylic is lighter and machine washable. Total yardage is about 500 g chunky. The dc stitch in chunky produces a very tight fabric with few gaps, so it keeps draughts out."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "Chunky wool or acrylic yarn",
              "qty": "500 g"
            },
            {
              "name": "8 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "9 dc x 10 rows = 10 x 10 cm in chunky yarn with an 8 mm hook. At this gauge a foundation chain of 81 gives a 90 cm finished width. In chunky yarn gauge varies significantly between brands, so swatch carefully before starting the full chain."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "ch: chain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "dc (UK) / sc (US): double crochet, the single stitch used throughout"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundation chain: chain 81."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 1: Dc into the 2nd ch from hook and every remaining ch. Turn. (80 dc.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Row 2 onward: Work a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "turning-chain"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "turning chain"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " of ch 1 (does not count as a stitch). Dc into every stitch across. Turn. (80 dc.)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Repeat Row 2 until piece measures 110 cm (approximately 110 rows). Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Edging (optional)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work one round of dc (UK) around the perimeter: 1 dc into each stitch along top and bottom, 1 dc into each row end on sides, 3 dc into each corner. This squares the edges."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "weaving-in-ends"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "weaving in ends"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to secure both tails. Wool: steam block lightly. Acrylic: lay flat, no heat needed."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Wool: handwash cool, squeeze dry in a towel, dry flat. Acrylic: machine wash 40 degrees, tumble dry low."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What to try next"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Try the same yarn weight with a shell stitch to add texture, or the basketweave throw in aran weight for a lighter version with a woven surface."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}